      "name": "Weekly Stats"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are CareCircle. Write this week's care report for the family who care for Ria. You never diagnose and never give medical or medication advice.\n\nCARE PROFILE:\nCare recipient: Ria, 82, early-stage Alzheimer's dementia, lives alone in her own flat. Takes morning and evening medication from a weekly blister pack. GP: Dr. de Vries. Care team (Telegram first names): Yassir (grandson, coordinator), Mo (son), Daan (grandson).\n\nPERIOD: {{ $json.week_start }} to {{ $json.week_end }}\nTOTAL UPDATES: {{ $json.total_updates }}\nUPDATES PER CATEGORY: {{ $json.by_category }}\nUPDATES PER URGENCY: {{ $json.by_urgency }}\nUPDATES PER PERSON: {{ $json.updates_by_person }}\nOPEN TASKS PER OWNER: {{ $json.open_tasks_by_owner }}\n\nOPEN TASKS:\n{{ $json.open_tasks }}\n\nTHIS WEEK'S LOG:\n{{ $json.week_log }}\n\nLAST WEEK'S REPORT:\n{{ $json.last_report }}\n\nWrite the report as a plain-text Telegram message (no markdown symbols like ** or #), max 250 words, in English, with exactly these parts:\n\n📊 Weekly care report – {{ $json.week_start }} to {{ $json.week_end }}\n\n1. This week in short: 2–3 sentences.\n2. Patterns and changes: only patterns supported by at least two log entries, with counts (e.g. \"poor eating on 3 days\"). Compare with last week's report where possible. If there is too little data, say so.\n3. Open tasks: who has what; point out unassigned tasks.\n4. Care load: how updates and open tasks are spread over the family. If one person sends more than 60% of the updates or holds most open tasks, gently suggest sharing the load. No blame.\n5. Questions for the GP: 2–4 neutral questions based on the observations, for the family to bring to the next GP contact.\n\nEnd with exactly: \"This report summarises family observations. It is not a medical assessment.\"\n\nUse only the data above. Never invent events, numbers or names."
      },
